            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="details" id="answer-1" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-1" hidden>
            <p>
              Cats often purr when they are relaxed, but purring can also happen
              when they are stressed, healing, or asking for comfort. Look at the
              rest of their body language to understand the mood behind it.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-2" id="question-2">
            <span>How much sleep do cats need?</span>
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="details" id="answer-2" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-2" hidden>
            <p>
              Most adult cats sleep around 12 to 16 hours a day, and kittens or
              senior cats may sleep even more. Short bursts of play between naps
              help satisfy their natural hunting rhythm.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-3" id="question-3">
            <span>Why does my cat knead blankets?</span>
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="details" id="answer-3" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-3" hidden>
            <p>
              Kneading is a comforting behavior that begins when kittens nurse.
              Adult cats may knead soft surfaces when they feel content, mark a
              resting spot with scent glands in their paws, or settle in for a nap.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-4" id="question-4">
            <span>Do indoor cats need enrichment?</span>
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="details" id="answer-4" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-4" hidden>
            <p>
              Yes. Scratching posts, window perches, puzzle feeders, climbing
              spaces, and daily interactive play give indoor cats healthy outlets
              for climbing, hunting, hiding, and exploring.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-5" id="question-5">
            <span>How can I tell if a cat is comfortable?</span>
            <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="details" id="answer-5" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-5" hidden>
            <p>
